# tgrmap, the TIGER map viewer of ipl_gpacks (tiger), on town.lch, a small synthetic map in its line chain format (beside it, made by
# officer_06's make_town_lch.py): opened through its own dialog, zoomed by a sweep, reset, zoomed and shifted by keys, a line identified
# with the right button, a street found by name, the layers asked for (at 24 bits it has no mutable colours and says so), the displayed part
# saved as t.lch, quit with q. Each dialog stands in the middle of the 870 by 870 window and takes keys with the pointer inside it.
# the opening dialog: the map file's name
move 435 437
type town.lch
key Return
wait
# a left sweep zooms onto the park
drag 1 300 250 600 450
wait
# 1 resets the whole map; + zooms by two; the left arrow shifts the centre
key 1
wait
key plus
wait
key Left
wait
key 1
wait
# the right button on Interstate 80 pops up the names under the pointer; r closes it and redraws
click 3 300 436
wait
move 435 437
key r
wait
# F finds a feature by name: Main St is drawn over in yellow
key F
wait
move 435 437
type main
key Return
wait
# L asks for the layers dialog; with no mutable colour it gives a notice, closed with Return
key L
wait
move 435 437
key Return
wait
# S saves the displayed portion through a file dialog
key S
wait
move 435 437
type t.lch
key Return
wait
# q quits
key q
